1
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:04,003
The math is all there.

2
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:06,131
-It's not real.
-Yes, it is.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:09,384
Look.
It is scientifically impossible

4
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:11,470
for a person to tip a cow.

5
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:14,181
Even you, with your stocky build

6
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:16,183
and lumberjack shoulders,
you couldn't do it.

7
00:00:17,643 --> 00:00:20,020
It's horrible. Why would you push
a cow over? They're sacred.

8
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:21,271
Oh, stop it.

9
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,273
I've seen you eat,
like, a million hamburgers.

10
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:26,151
Hey, an animal can be both
sacred and delicious.

11
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,029
Look, I'm telling you
I've done it, okay?

12
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:30,781
I clearly remember
the cow standing up

13
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,282
and then the cow on its side.

14
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,243
Were you drunk?

15
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:37,788
I was 16 in Nebraska.
What do you think?

16
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,707
I think you're the one who fell over.

17
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:44,836
That would explain why the sky
was also on its side.

18
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:47,464
-Hey.
-Howard.

19
00:00:47,673 --> 00:00:48,840
Cow tipping: real or not?

20
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:51,301
I'm going to say... not.

21
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,470
That's just based on me
trying to roll

22
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:55,806
my mom over
when she's snoring.

23
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:59,851
Speaking of that big side of beef,

24
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:03,355
she's invited all of you
to Thanksgiving at her house.

25
00:01:03,814 --> 00:01:05,023
Mmm.

26
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:08,026
You know, I've been told
that a bald refusal

27
00:01:08,235 --> 00:01:10,362
of an invitation is rude
and one must instead

28
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:12,197
offer up a polite excuse, so...

29
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,658
I'd love to go, but, unfortunately,

30
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,743
that sounds awful.

31
00:01:20,122 --> 00:01:21,873
Come on, it'll be fun.

32
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,208
We were actually
going to do it here.

33
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:24,876
Please?
Bernadette's bringing her dad,

34
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:26,253
because her mom's out of town,

35
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:28,213
and I never have anything
to say to that guy.

36
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:30,632
Since you put it that way,
I'd love to go,

37
00:01:30,841 --> 00:01:32,551
but that sounds even more awful.

38
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:34,845
It'd actually be nice to not hear

39
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:36,680
Sheldon complain
about my cooking all day.

40
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:38,015
SHELDON: Excuse me,

41
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,892
but every year
you prepare a terrible meal

42
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,020
and every year I criticize it.

43
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,564
Do our traditions
mean nothing to you?

44
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,026
-I want to go.
-Yeah, me, too.

45
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:50,402
-I'm in.
-Sheldon.

46
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:52,863
(GROANS) Fine, I'll go.

47
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:55,282
But if her food is delicious,
Thanksgiving is ruined,

48
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:56,658
and it's on you.

49
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:00,746
(THEME SONG PLAYS)

50
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:25,270
Do we really have to go
to Mrs. Wolowitz's house?

51
00:02:25,604 --> 00:02:26,647
We do.

52
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:27,898
The Thanksgiving Decoupling

53
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,566
And I expect you
to be on your best behavior.

54
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:33,028
Now I know how the
African slaves felt.

55
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:35,989
Being dragged from their homes

56
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:39,368
to labor under the
yoke of the white man.

57
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:42,537
Are you honestly comparing
Thanksgiving dinner

58
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:45,332
at Wolowitz's mom's with
one of the greatest tragedies

59
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,250
in the history of mankind?

60
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:49,168
Yes.

61
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:52,214
Sheldon, you can have
a nice Thanksgiving anywhere.

62
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:53,674
I spent one in Vegas.

63
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:55,759
You did?

64
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:57,386
Yeah, back when I was dating Zack.

65
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,137
It was actually more fun
than I thought.

66
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:01,682
We gambled, we went to one
of those cheesy wedding chapels,

67
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,308
we had a really good
turkey dinner.

68
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:06,019
Which was surprising,
since we were at a strip club.

69
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,355
Wait, you went to a chapel?

70
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:09,731
-Yeah.
-Why?

71
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,859
We had one of those
silly fake weddings.

72
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:18,281
Penny...

73
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,492
you know those are real, right?

74
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:22,119
No, they're not.

75
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:25,038
Yeah, they are.

76
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,124
No, they're not.

77
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,251
Yeah, they are.

78
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:30,752
-He's right.
-They're real.

79
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:35,507
But it... didn't seem real.

80
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:37,634
Let me ask you a question.

81
00:03:37,843 --> 00:03:42,597
At any point,
was Las Vegas on its side?

82
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,479
-Hi, Dad.
-Hi, honey. Mm.

83
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:53,358
Oh, you brought beer
for everybody.

84
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:57,070
Okay.
Yeah, it's for everybody.

85
00:03:58,447 --> 00:04:00,949
I really just wanted to have
a nice, quiet day at home

86
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:02,284
and watch the game.

87
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:05,495
You can have a quiet day
and watch the game here.

88
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:09,207
MOTHER: Howard,
the medicine's not working!

89
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:12,711
HOWARD: You just took it.

90
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:15,464
At least let it
reach your first stomach!

91
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,218
Hey, Mike.

92
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:21,470
Let me help you out, there.

93
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,638
Thanks.
What's wrong with your mom?

94
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:25,015
Oh, her gout's flaring up.

95
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:28,393
Turns out an apple pie a day
does not keep the doctor away.

96
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:32,856
MOTHER: How can
one little toe hurt so bad?

97
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:37,903
Maybe because that little piggy
is being crushed by the barn!

98
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,573
She should quiet down soon.

99
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:44,785
I gave her enough pain meds
to choke a... well, her.

100
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,872
I guess we're going to
have to do all the cooking.

101
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,123
I have a better idea.

102
00:04:50,332 --> 00:04:51,416
If you think you're
going to make me

103
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:52,876
do all this by myself,
you're crazy.

104
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,711
I was going to make Raj
do it all by himself.

105
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,421
Oh, well, that's a great idea.

106
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:01,802
No traffic, we're sailing.

107
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,971
Yes. Like we're on a ship.

108
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:08,016
Coming from Africa to America.

109
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,771
Sheldon, that's
completely inappropriate.

110
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,857
You can't keep comparing
yourself to a slave.

111
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,527
Yes, Miss Amy.

112
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:23,406
I can't believe you're
married to that idiot.

113
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:25,826
Would you stop?
We just did it as a goof.

114
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,369
Well, a goof or not,
you're actually married.

115
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,162
You need to get
this taken care of.

116
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:31,623
I will. Why are you
making this such a big deal?

117
00:05:31,832 --> 00:05:33,792
Oh! I have a reason.

118
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,670
It could be because
you said yes to marrying Zack,

119
00:05:36,878 --> 00:05:38,380
but every time
Leonard's proposed,

120
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:40,090
he's gotten a resounding no.

121
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:45,053
That's just off the top of my head.

122
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:46,847
So how do I undo this?

123
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,431
I'm hoping you can
get an annulment,

124
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,933
so it's just like
it never happened.

125
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:51,643
Great, well, what do I have to do?

126
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:53,270
It says here
you can get an annulment

127
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:55,146
if any of the following
conditions are met.

128
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:57,107
"Were you unable
to consummate the marriage?"

129
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:58,984
(LAUGHS)
Penny? Next.

130
00:06:01,111 --> 00:06:03,572
"Is there any evidence
of fraud, bigamy,

131
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,073
want of understanding?"

132
00:06:05,282 --> 00:06:07,242
'Want of understanding?'
What does that even mean?

133
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,160
Ding, ding, ding.
We have a winner.

134
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,747
Thanks for saving the day.

135
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:13,999
No problem.

136
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,250
It wouldn't be Thanksgiving

137
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:18,628
without an Indian
providing the food.

138
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:22,340
Now, where does your mom
keep the Crisco?

139
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:23,592
I don't know.

140
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,594
Probably in a wad in her cheek.

141
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,764
I'll help Raj in here.
Why don't you go keep my dad company?

142
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:32,225
Oh, he doesn't want me in there.
I'm the creepy little guy

143
00:06:32,434 --> 00:06:34,728
who has sex with his daughter.

144
00:06:36,897 --> 00:06:39,149
-Don't be silly, he loves you.
-Does he?

145
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:41,693
-Okay, he cares about you a lot.
-Really?

146
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:44,988
I do crap for you all the time.
Get out there.

147
00:06:50,619 --> 00:06:53,830
So your wife's in Arizona
with the grandkids?

148
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,290
Uh-huh.

149
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,462
You know, my mom's been to Arizona.

150
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,173
She rode one of those mules
down in the Grand Canyon.

151
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:06,051
Long story short,
they had to shoot it.

152
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:12,515
Because she's so fat.

153
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,811
(DOORBELL RINGS)

154
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,481
I'll get the door
while you finish laughing.

155
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:25,070
-Hey, guys.
-Happy Thanksgiving.

156
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,655
It smells wonderful.

157
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,907
Is anyone slaving away
in the kitchen?

158
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,575
-Because I, too, know--
-Sheldon.

159
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,329
Here. Thank you for having us.

160
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:35,580
What's with you?

161
00:07:35,789 --> 00:07:36,831
She's mad at me

162
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,000
because she just found out
she's married to Zack.

163
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:40,585
Really?

164
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:42,045
That dumb-ass you used to date?

165
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:44,673
That's hysterical.

166
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:48,343
I can't believe I felt bad
for opening this in the car.

167
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:55,350
You need any help?

168
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,769
Yeah, can you reach
that gravy boat up there?

169
00:07:58,061 --> 00:07:59,229
-Uh, sure.
-Great.

170
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:00,689
That makes one of you.

171
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:06,236
Okay we have a lot to do
and not much time to do it.

172
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:08,822
Bernadette, you're on corn,
gravy and yam detail.

173
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:10,240
Amy, you're on rolls, cranberries

174
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:12,784
and making sure Bernadette stays
away from the marshmallows.

175
00:08:13,994 --> 00:08:15,829
That's right, I see you.

176
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:18,790
Okay if you have
any questions,

177
00:08:18,999 --> 00:08:20,750
I'll be over here
basting my ass off.

178
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,377
Focus is key.

179
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:25,505
Did you guys know Penny
married Zack three years ago?

180
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:27,507
-What?
-Wha...?

181
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,222
You ever play football?

182
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:35,849
A little in college.

183
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:38,018
-You?
-No.

184
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:40,895
But I did get tackled
in the hallway once.

185
00:08:42,731 --> 00:08:45,608
The whole school cheered.

186
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,320
I found the, court papers

187
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,864
that you and Zack
need to fill out.

188
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,657
-I'll print them when we get home.
-Fine.

189
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,701
And we can just put this
whole thing behind us.

190
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:55,952
Are you done?

191
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:57,746
-What?
-Look, I get it, I screwed up.

192
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,497
Is this all we're going to talk
about the rest of the day?

193
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:00,749
Why are you mad at me?

194
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,125
You're the one that
did the stupid thing.

195
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:05,086
-I'm just trying to fix it.
-(GROANS) I need some air.

196
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:06,880
Well... Penny.

197
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:08,757
Now, I don't know the
first thing about women,

198
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,800
but I would not follow her.

199
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:16,014
Listen to Stretch.

200
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,103
How am I the bad guy?

201
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,856
She's the one who married
someone else. I'm the victim.

202
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:28,109
Sounds like Zack's the victim.
You're sleeping with his wife.

203
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,740
I've kept my marriage
together for 35 years.

204
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:36,326
-Can I weigh in here?
-Sure.

205
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:38,620
I'm trying to watch the game.
Shut up.

206
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:41,915
(GROANS)

207
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:44,459
How do you not make
a first down there?

208
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:46,252
They passed against
a nickel defense.

209
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:48,254
They should have run it off-tackle.

210
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:52,675
How the hell
do you know that?

211
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:54,302
My father loved football.

212
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:56,054
He always made me watch it

213
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,806
before I was allowed
to do my homework.

214
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,682
(DOOR OPENS)
PENNY: Well...

215
00:09:59,891 --> 00:10:01,351
You'll be happy to know
I just spoke to Zack

216
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,019
and he's willing to
sign the court papers.

217
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:04,354
He's on his way here now.

218
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:07,190
-Wait, you invited him here?
-Yeah.

219
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:09,025
I'm getting ready
to weigh in again.

220
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:10,360
Come on.

221
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,405
What do you think
they ought to do now?

222
00:10:14,613 --> 00:10:16,699
I would throw a quick slant
to a wide-out,

223
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:19,160
given that the defense
is showing blitz.

224
00:10:19,369 --> 00:10:22,497
Oh, I love a good blitz,
especially with sour cream.

225
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:27,210
Get it?

226
00:10:27,418 --> 00:10:29,254
Because it sounds like "blintz."

227
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,549
MOTHER: Did someone say blintz?

228
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:35,927
I just don't understand
why you invited him here today.

229
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,345
Because you wouldn't
shut up about it.

230
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,597
When I called him, he had nothing to do,
so I just thought it would--

231
00:10:39,806 --> 00:10:41,349
Hey, guys, I'm trying
to cook in here.

232
00:10:41,558 --> 00:10:42,725
Oh, sorry.
We'll keep it down.

233
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,769
No, no, speak up.

234
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:46,896
I'm about to use the blender,

235
00:10:47,105 --> 00:10:48,898
and I don't want to miss anything.

236
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:51,651
Well, you might have
to cook for one more

237
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,902
because she invited Zack.

238
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:54,946
-AMY: What?
-BERNADETTE: What?

239
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:57,699
My, my.

240
00:10:57,907 --> 00:11:01,494
The plot, like my gravy, thickens.

241
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,792
I don't care for your
mother's bathroom.

242
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:10,003
There's not an angle
to do one's business

243
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:12,881
without a clown figurine
staring at you.

244
00:11:14,299 --> 00:11:18,720
-That's why I sit.
-Yeah, that's why.

245
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:23,266
You remember
the Thanksgiving game

246
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,268
when it snowed in Dallas?

247
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:28,897
Nineteen-ninety three. Leon Lett blew
the game in the final seconds

248
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,857
and the Dolphins
emerged victorious.

249
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,860
Then I finally got to do
my calculus.

250
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:37,322
I was so pissed,
I wanted to shoot my TV.

251
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,282
So was my dad.

252
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,575
And then he did.

253
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:44,370
-Anyone need a beer?
-Yeah.

254
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:45,997
Thank God.

255
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:49,708
So, does your dad
still live in Texas?

256
00:11:49,918 --> 00:11:52,545
No.
He died when I was 14.

257
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,465
I'm sorry to hear that.

258
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:57,926
So was the man who owned
the local liquor store.

259
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:01,596
He cried and cried.

260
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:05,683
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

261
00:12:06,601 --> 00:12:09,229
So, if your dad died
when you were 14,

262
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:12,190
you were never old enough
to have a beer with the man.

263
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:13,608
No, sir.

264
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:16,611
He did try to give me one
for my high school graduation,

265
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:19,030
but I was 11 and my mom said, no.

266
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,162
Well, you're having one with me.

267
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,502
All right.

268
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:36,422
To your dad.

269
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:43,638
I never had a beer
with my dad, either.

270
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:49,352
Do you mind?
We're having a moment here.

271
00:12:57,568 --> 00:12:59,654
I can't believe Penny's
married to Zack.

272
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:01,322
I wonder what she saw in that guy.

273
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:02,824
I don't know.

274
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,826
He's sweet, he's tall, handsome.

275
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,536
Broad shoulders, good hair.

276
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:08,621
Hmm, wonder what she
sees in Leonard.

277
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,918
How's it going out there?

278
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:17,505
Sheldon and your dad are bonding
and completely ignoring me.

279
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,757
I know how you feel.

280
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:23,261
Sheldon ignored me for a week
when he got that Roomba vacuum.

281
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:27,348
I kick it when he's not looking.

282
00:13:29,559 --> 00:13:30,601
What are they doing?

283
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:33,313
They're drinking beer
and watching football.

284
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,148
So why don't you do that
with them?

285
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:37,650
-They don't want me.
-What do you mean?

286
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:41,404
Well, Sheldon started talking
about how his dad isn't alive anymore,

287
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:42,905
and they were toasting,
and I tried to tell them

288
00:13:43,114 --> 00:13:44,782
about how sad I was
when my dad abandoned--

289
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:46,576
(DOORBELL RINGS)
Zack's here!

290
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:48,911
Stir the gravy.

291
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,458
Sorry. I really want
to hear how sad you are.

292
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,710
I'll be back in, like, five, ten minutes.

293
00:14:00,715 --> 00:14:02,800
Sorry she made you come
over here on a holiday.

294
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:04,886
It's all right.
I didn't have anything going on.

295
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:06,471
Plus, Penny told me we're married,

296
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:09,140
and Thanksgiving's a time
to be with family.

297
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:12,685
Yeah, okay great.
Can we just get this over with?

298
00:14:12,894 --> 00:14:15,313
Yeah, you guys
have to sign here and here.

299
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,148
On Monday,
we'll file for the annulment,

300
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:18,816
and this "marriage" will be over.

301
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:20,068
Okay.

302
00:14:21,361 --> 00:14:22,862
I don't know if I want to sign it.

303
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:24,739
ALL: Ooh!

304
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:28,242
Why won't you sign it?

305
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:31,704
I just think splitting up
can be rough on kids.

306
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,123
We don't have any kids.

307
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:35,750
Are you sure?
Because you didn't know

308
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,752
we were married
until this morning.

309
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,297
Okay, look, Zack, come on.

310
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:43,466
You know neither of us
thought this was real.

311
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:45,676
I mean, we were married
by an Elvis impersonator.

312
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,220
Of course it was an impersonator.

313
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:50,098
We could never afford
a real Elvis.

314
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:55,436
You married him instead of me?

315
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,230
Good call.

316
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:58,815
Sign the papers.

317
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:00,108
Hang on.
You know what?

318
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,984
You have been a jerk
about this all day.

319
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:03,486
You always do this!
Whenever I mess up,

320
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,363
you're right there to make me
feel even worse about it.

321
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,740
-That is not true.
-We could've waited till Monday,

322
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:09,283
signed the papers,
this all would have been over.

323
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:10,868
You're the one who
invited him here.

324
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:12,120
There you go again.
Just another mistake

325
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:13,496
you're throwing in my face.

326
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,456
Not cool, bro.

327
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,501
I'm starting to think

328
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:21,254
you're not the kind of guy
I want dating my wife.

329
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:26,592
Yeah, well, she's not going to
be your wife for long.

330
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:28,386
Oh, no.
Are you dying?

331
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:32,098
I'm about to.
Sign the paper.

332
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:38,396
Know what they say:
"Happy wife, happy life."

333
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:40,731
Let's eat.

334
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:49,532
(BELCHING) Two, three,
eight, four, six.

335
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:54,370
That's all I can do
without throwing up.

336
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,081
That is not what I expected

337
00:15:57,290 --> 00:16:00,251
when you said you
were going to burp "pi."

338
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:04,422
MOTHER: Did somebody say pie?

339
00:16:05,423 --> 00:16:06,841
I don't know what's scarier:

340
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:08,342
the bathroom clowns,

341
00:16:08,551 --> 00:16:11,345
or the woman
that put them there.

342
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:15,558
All I know is you can
only fit one of her in a car.

343
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:20,646
And there's the clown
that came out of her.

344
00:16:26,027 --> 00:16:28,321
I really didn't want
to come here,

345
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:30,239
but this is shaping up to be

346
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:32,783
one of the best Thanksgivings
I've had in a long time.

347
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,494
Me, too.

348
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,663
Hey. Howard says you've
been making fun of him all day!

349
00:16:37,872 --> 00:16:40,708
Now, both of you apologize right now!

350
00:16:41,584 --> 00:16:43,252
She's so tiny.

351
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,550
It's funny when she's mad.

352
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:54,472
All right, mister, I think you owe

353
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:57,517
Howard and Bernadette an apology.

354
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:00,144
Perhaps you're right.

355
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:03,814
I'm sorry for my behavior.

356
00:17:04,022 --> 00:17:05,983
I've had alcohol,
and it's caused me

357
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:07,235
to be inappropriate.

358
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,237
-It's okay.
-Don't worry about it.

359
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,821
Thank you.

360
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,865
Ain't she great?

361
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:14,992
Sheldon.

362
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:17,453
Now, how's about you get
us a couple of beers?

363
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,092
Thanks again for cooking.

364
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,593
Yeah, everything was delicious.

365
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:36,681
Well, I couldn't have done it
without my two favorite girls.

366
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:39,559
Martha Stewart and Rachael Ray.

367
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:45,815
Hey, Sheldon,
what do you say we go outside

368
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:48,067
and throw around the old pigskin?

369
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:50,278
This is a Jewish house.

370
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,697
I don't think they have pigskin.

371
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,285
MOTHER: Did someone say pigskin?

372
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:01,372
Hey, I'm sorry about today.

373
00:18:01,581 --> 00:18:03,499
And I promise,
next time I get married,

374
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:04,792
it won't be a joke.

375
00:18:05,001 --> 00:18:06,711
It'll be for love.

376
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:08,546
Or money.

377
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:13,134
I'm sorry, too.

378
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:15,094
Don't be.
It's my fault.

379
00:18:15,303 --> 00:18:16,762
I was a terrible husband.

380
00:18:18,389 --> 00:18:20,600
I was never around.

381
00:18:22,852 --> 00:18:24,687
I know I'm hard on you,

382
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:27,481
but you're not the worst
son-in-law in the world.

383
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:30,401
Mike, that's the nicest thing
you've ever said to me.

384
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,154
Well, I'm drunk.

385
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,452
I just vomited on a lot of clowns.

